    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30067" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">murrĕus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">murrhĕus, myr-rhĕus</span></b> ),
			a, um, adj.
		3. murra, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the stone
				murra, murrean</i>: pocula,
			<i>made of murra</i>, <i><span class="en">Prop. 4</span></i>
			(5), 5, 26: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">poculum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 119, 3</span></i>
			.‡ † <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">murrhacŏpum</span></b> , i, n.,
			= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μύρραἄκοπον</span>, <i>a
				medicament compounded with myrrh, for removing weariness</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">acopum murrhacopum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Not. Tir. p. 160</span></i>
			.</div>
